  "context_pill": "Section 35AD & Section 73A",
  "example_summary": "Mr. A sets up three warehousing facilities (food grains, sugar, and edible oil) and we must determine the tax treatment for each, specifically focusing on Section 35AD deductions for specified businesses and the ring-fencing of losses under Section 73A.",
  "source_provision": "### Master Statutory Summary Matrix\n\n| Business Activity / Nature | Statutory Section | Capital Expenditure Treatment | Eligible Tax Consequence & Loss Rule |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Specified Business (Warehousing for Agriculture/Sugar)** | Section 35AD | 100% deduction for capital expenditure incurred (excluding land) | 100% deduction allowed; Losses can be carried forward indefinitely and set-off only against specified business profits u/s 73A |\n| **Non-Specified Business (Warehousing for Edible Oil)** | Section 32 | Capital expenditure capitalized; eligible for standard depreciation | Depreciation allowed (e.g. 10% for buildings); Normal business profit/loss treatment |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Section 35AD Exclusion: Expenditure on acquisition of land does not qualify for deduction under Section 35AD.\n\n\n> [!WARNING] Section 73A Restriction: Loss from a specified business can be set-off only against profits from another specified business and cannot be set-off against non-specified business profits.",
